  "criteria": "1) Output tokens per request and total output tokens over time per ModelId, to confirm that growth is tokens-per-request and not volume. 2) Which models and which callers (IAM principals, applications, or log-derived fields) account for the growth. 3) Evidence of runaway or verbose output: raised or missing max_tokens, reasoning/extended-thinking models, prompt or system-prompt changes, agent loops or retries, a switch to a more expensive model, or a shift in pricing tier. 4) Whether prompt caching is in use or missing. 5) Reconcile CloudWatch token counts against Cost Explorer Bedrock spend and flag any mismatch. 6) Any changes (CloudTrail, deployments) that line up with the start of the drift. 7) Concrete, quantified savings opportunities (cap max_tokens, cheaper model, caching, batch or flex tier, etc.). Use read-only calls only. Clearly state what you could not access (e.g. invocation logging disabled, no Cost Explorer permission) and which conclusions are inferred vs. directly evidenced. Return concise findings with numbers, model IDs, and timestamps."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Deep analysis of Bedrock output-token cost growth"}], "created_at": null}

